meta {
  name: Lead Pull - Staged Leads
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/lead-pull/runs/{{leadPullRunId}}/leads?tenant_id={{tenantId}}&verdict=new&page=1&page_size=50
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  The staged rows behind each summary number. ?verdict= is optional — omit it for
  every row.

  CONTACT VALUES ARE DELIBERATELY NOT RETURNED. The grid needs a verdict, the
  Meta ids and the form name to be actionable; it does not need the phone number
  and email of someone who has not been imported yet, and returning them would
  put un-consented PII into a screen, a browser cache and every proxy log on the
  way there.

  Two columns carry the ONE DELIBERATE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE from the Python:
    is_hiring_form              the form name matches hiring|recruit|vacancy|
                                career|job application|sales exe
    suggested_campaign_type_id  what marketing.fn_match_campaign_type matched on
    (+ suggested_campaign_type_label)

  In meta-sync-scripts/common/reconcile.py `hiring_form` was a SKIP verdict,
  because a job applicant had nowhere to go. Since campaign types (1.49.0) it
  does, so it stopped being a verdict: these leads now CLASSIFY AND IMPORT
  NORMALLY, and the admin is pointed at the real fix — setting
  ext.meta_page_form_org_map.default_campaign_type_id on that page/form.

  Regression check the unmapped case explicitly (?verdict=unmapped_form):
    * a lead on a form with no mapping row must appear here with org_id NULL and
      a reason naming the form id
    * it must also appear in the run's verdict_summary
    * Apply must SKIP it with applied_error 'unmapped_form' and must never guess
      a branch — one Page here is shared by eight branch orgs, so "the page's
      org" is not a well-defined thing.

  Regression checks:
    * a run id from tenant B, requested as tenant A -> 404
    * an unknown verdict value -> 422
    * caller below super_admin -> 403
}
